        "decision": "keep",
        "effect": "invalid_execution",
        "reason": "Case 4 indexes the 5-element whences array with byte%6, so index 5 reads out of bounds. A 3-byte input reaches it whether or not gzopen succeeds. This is a preexisting harness defect and counts under J2.",
        "finite_witness": "Bytes 00 04 05. mode_sz=2, so 1 byte is copied into mode and data is not advanced. The op byte 0x04 selects case 4. dataLen is 1, so the next byte 0x05 gives 5%6=5 and the harness reads whences[5].",
        "scope_contract": {
          "status": "established",
          "reason": "The seek operation is one of the harness's primary operations; it calls gzseek with the decoded whence.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "unit_id": "u-1ff4587e1cb89bf573f9",
              "start_line": 79,
              "end_line": 86,
              "role": "primary",
              "dependency_reason": "Seek operation and whence decoding."
